Local mitigation patch, not upstream: mitodl/keycloak-scim's
ScimEventListenerProvider.onEvent(AdminEvent, boolean) NullPointerExceptions on every
single Admin-API user DELETE. getUser(userId) looks the user up by ID to check
isEmailVerified() before dispatching the SCIM delete, but by the time the DELETE admin
event fires, Keycloak has already removed that row -- getUser() always returns null, and
the unchecked user.isEmailVerified() call throws unconditionally.

Fix: drop the isEmailVerified() gate for DELETE and dispatch unconditionally, matching
how the plugin's own EventType.DELETE_ACCOUNT branch (self-service delete, a few lines
above in the same file) already handles this with no such gate. ScimClient.delete()
already no-ops safely for a user that was never synced (its own JPA mapping-table lookup
catches NoResultException and logs "scim mapping not found" instead of throwing), so
removing the redundant, broken pre-check here is safe.

Verified against a live Keycloak + this plugin: without this patch, every Admin-API user
delete throws (KC-SERVICES0085, NullPointerException at ScimEventListenerProvider.java:87)
and no DELETE ever reaches the SCIM service provider. With this patch applied, the DELETE
event correctly dispatches through to the configured SCIM endpoint.

Filed upstream: https://github.com/mitodl/keycloak-scim/issues/181, fix proposed at
https://github.com/mitodl/keycloak-scim/pull/182 -- remove this patch and the
`git apply` step in Dockerfile.keycloak-scim once that (or an equivalent fix) lands
and this harness's pinned KEYCLOAK_SCIM_COMMIT moves past it.

--- a/src/main/java/sh/libre/scim/event/ScimEventListenerProvider.java
+++ b/src/main/java/sh/libre/scim/event/ScimEventListenerProvider.java
@@ -83,10 +83,7 @@
                 }
             }
             if (event.getOperationType() == OperationType.DELETE) {
-                var user = getUser(userId);
-                if (user.isEmailVerified()) {
-                    dispatcher.run(ScimDispatcher.SCOPE_USER, client -> client.delete(UserAdapter.class, userId));
-                }
+                dispatcher.run(ScimDispatcher.SCOPE_USER, client -> client.delete(UserAdapter.class, userId));
             }
         }
         if (event.getResourceType() == ResourceType.GROUP) {
